Engineering Architecture Guide: Offloading Lambda Outbound Security (mTLS & TLS) to Istio Egress GatewayThis document outlines how to design an architecture where an AWS Lambda function relies entirely on an EKS-based Istio Egress Gateway to connect to on-premises systems.By offloading the cryptographic handshakes and certificate management to Istio, the Lambda function requires no native IBM MQ client libraries, no crypto configurations, and no client certificates embedded in its deployment package.1. Architectural Overview                        ┌─────────────────── AWS VPC ───────────────────┐
